-- title:
--   Hecke–Galois datum at a level cube-free away from p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W\neq 0$ that is a semistable model (for every prime $q$ with $q\mid\Delta_W$ one has $q\nmid c_4(W)$) and whose mod $p$ representation is irreducible in the sense that the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is non-trivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $0$ and the whole module. Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number such that $q^3\nmid M$ for every prime $q\neq p$, such that $W$ is residually modular of level $M$ (there exist a normalised eigenform $f$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ containing $p$ with $a_\ell(f)$ integral and congruent to $a_\ell(W)$ mod $\mathfrak m$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M\Delta_W$, $\ell\neq p$), and such that $p^2\nmid M$ if $p\mid\Delta_W$ or $p\nmid a_p(W)$, while $p\nmid M$ if $p\nmid\Delta_W$ and $p\mid a_p(W)$; here $a_q(W)$ denotes $q+1$ minus the number of points of the reduction of $W$ mod $q$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field in which $p$ lies in the maximal ideal. Then there exist a finite set $S$ of primes containing $p$ and every prime dividing $\Delta_W$, and a non-zero level $N$, such that $M\mid N$, every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$, $q^2\mid N$ and $q^3\nmid N$ for every $q\in S$ with $q\neq p$, while $p\mid N$ and $p^2\nmid N$ if $p\mid \Delta_W$ or $p\nmid a_p(W)$, and $p\nmid N$ if $p\nmid\Delta_W$ and $p\mid a_p(W)$; moreover the weight $2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with rational integral $q$-expansion coefficients span the whole space over $\mathbb{C}$, and there are a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$ outside $S$ and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$ outside $S$) to the residue field of $\mathcal O$ with $\theta(T_\ell)$ the residue of $a_\ell(W)$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, and a complete local Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $T$, finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module with local structure morphism, admitting a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum N S 𝒪 θ T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8): a lift $\pi$ of $\theta$ to $T$ generating $T$ over $\mathcal O$, through which every $\mathcal O$-valued character of the Hecke algebra reducing to $\theta$ factors by an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $T\to\mathcal O$, with surjective residue map from $\mathcal O$, together with an adic Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ whose Frobenius at each prime $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ has characteristic polynomial $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible.
--
--   This is the level-raising hub of the Wiles argument in the form needed for the Frey curve: it packages the passage from residual modularity at some level $M$ to an auxiliary level $N$ adapted to a finite set $S$ of primes, together with the Hecke algebra, the residual eigensystem matching the Frobenius traces of $W$, and the universal Hecke–Galois datum over a finite free $\mathcal O$-algebra. It is the variant in which the starting level, and hence the constructed level, is cube-free away from $p$ (valuation exactly $2$ at the primes of $S\setminus\{p\}$), and it is used by the two subsequent statements that feed residual modularity with prescribed local behaviour into the modularity lifting step.
